From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yclu4 <yclu4@nuvoton.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm-backend: allocate hw cursor-plane GBM buffers under
 pixman renderer

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [BSP-specific: GC520 2D/direct-KMS-scanout hack, not upstreamable as-is]

Re-diffed against Weston 13.0.1 (was written and hand-tested against
10.0.5 for Buildroot); structurally identical porting to that version -
drm_output_init_cursor_egl()/drm_output_fini_cursor_egl() and the
drm_output_init_pixman()/drm_output_fini_pixman() call sites are
essentially unchanged between 10.0.5 and 13.0.1 (mostly cosmetic
struct/field renames elsewhere in the same functions).

drm_output_init_cursor_egl()/drm_output_fini_cursor_egl() were only ever
called from the EGL/GBM per-output init path (drm_output_init_egl(),
drm-gbm.c), so output->gbm_cursor_fb[] stayed NULL when running the
pixman renderer (our stack has no GL renderer). The first
wl_pointer.set_cursor() from a client would then dereference a NULL fb
in the cursor-plane placement path (state-propose.c).

Despite the _egl suffix, these functions only need b->gbm (already
created by init_pixman() for dmabuf import - see the drm/pixman dmabuf
patch) and require no EGL context. Make them non-static and call them
from drm_output_init_pixman()/drm_output_fini_pixman() so the hardware
cursor plane works under pixman too - at the same relative point in the
per-output lifecycle where drm_output_init_egl() already calls
drm_output_init_cursor_egl() for the GL path. Failure is non-fatal:
drm_output_init_cursor_egl() already sets b->cursors_are_broken on
error for a clean software-cursor fallback.
---
--- a/libweston/backend-drm/drm-gbm.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-drm/drm-gbm.c
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static void drm_output_fini_cursor_egl(struct drm_output *output)
+void drm_output_fini_cursor_egl(struct drm_output *output)
 {
 	unsigned int i;
 
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@
 	}
 }
 
-static int
+int
 drm_output_init_cursor_egl(struct drm_output *output, struct drm_backend *b)
 {
 	struct drm_device *device = output->device;
--- a/libweston/backend-drm/drm-internal.h
+++ b/libweston/backend-drm/drm-internal.h
@@ -995,6 +995,20 @@
 struct drm_fb *
 drm_output_render_gl(struct drm_output_state *state, pixman_region32_t *damage);
 
+/*
+ * Cursor-plane GBM buffer allocation. Despite the _egl suffix (kept for
+ * historical/naming consistency with drm_output_init_egl), these only need
+ * b->gbm (a plain GBM device used for dumb/cursor BO allocation) and do NOT
+ * require an EGL context. They are therefore also usable from the pixman
+ * renderer's per-output init path (drm_output_init_pixman()) as long as
+ * init_pixman() has already created b->gbm - see drm.c.
+ */
+int
+drm_output_init_cursor_egl(struct drm_output *output, struct drm_backend *b);
+
+void
+drm_output_fini_cursor_egl(struct drm_output *output);
+
 #else
 inline static int
 init_egl(struct drm_backend *b)
@@ -1014,6 +1028,17 @@
 {
 }
 
+inline static int
+drm_output_init_cursor_egl(struct drm_output *output, struct drm_backend *b)
+{
+	return -1;
+}
+
+inline static void
+drm_output_fini_cursor_egl(struct drm_output *output)
+{
+}
+
 inline static struct drm_fb *
 drm_output_render_gl(struct drm_output_state *state, pixman_region32_t *damage)
 {
--- a/libweston/backend-drm/drm.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-drm/drm.c
@@ -1639,6 +1639,18 @@
 	weston_log("DRM: output %s %s shadow framebuffer.\n", output->base.name,
 		   b->use_pixman_shadow ? "uses" : "does not use");
 
+	/* Allocate cursor-plane scratch GBM buffers so the hardware cursor
+	 * plane can be used under the pixman renderer too.
+	 * drm_output_init_cursor_egl() only needs b->gbm (already created by
+	 * init_pixman() above for dmabuf import) - it does not require an
+	 * EGL context, despite the name. Without this, output->gbm_cursor_fb[]
+	 * stays NULL and the first wl_pointer.set_cursor() from a client
+	 * would dereference a NULL fb in the DRM backend's cursor-plane
+	 * path. Failure here is non-fatal: drm_output_init_cursor_egl()
+	 * already sets b->cursors_are_broken on error, causing clean
+	 * fallback to a software (blitted) cursor. */
+	drm_output_init_cursor_egl(output, b);
+
 	return 0;
 
 err:
@@ -1678,6 +1690,8 @@
 		output->renderbuffer[i] = NULL;
 	}
 
+	drm_output_fini_cursor_egl(output);
+
 	renderer->pixman->output_destroy(&output->base);
 }
 
